  "body": "Positioned on the 15th floor of the iconic Spencer Apartments, this is your opportunity to enjoy one of Takapuna's most sought after lifestyles. Take in breathtaking views across Rangitoto Island, the Hauraki Gulf and Auckland's sparkling skyline, all from the comfort of your own apartment.\r\nLight filled and thoughtfully designed, the open plan living area flows effortlessly, while the dedicated study space provides the perfect spot to work from home, catch up on emails or simply soak in the ever changing outlook.\r\n\r\nWhy you'll love living here:\r\n* Spectacular views across Rangitoto Island, the Hauraki Gulf and Auckland's city skyline\r\n* Light filled open plan living with a dedicated study space\r\n* Resort style facilities including a heated swimming pool, spa, full size tennis court and Technogym fitness centre\r\n* Takapuna Beach just a short stroll away\r\n* Boutique shopping, cafés, award winning restaurants and the Sunday Market all within easy walking distance\r\n* Opposite the Takapuna Bowling Club\r\n* Ideal first home, investment or lock up and leave lifestyle\r\n\r\nLiving at The Spencer is about more than just owning an apartment. It's about enjoying an enviable coastal lifestyle where everything you need is within walking distance and every day feels a little more like a holiday.\r\nFinding this combination of views, location and resort style amenities is becoming increasingly difficult. This apartment offers exceptional buying for those wanting to secure a foothold in one of Auckland's most desirable seaside suburbs.\r\nA rare opportunity also exists to purchase the apartment directly above. Whether you're looking to secure two investments, accommodate extended family or simply explore the possibilities, contact Team Rogers to discuss this unique offering.\r\nThe vendor's instructions are clear. This apartment will be sold. Opportunities like this don't stay available for long. Contact Team Rogers today before someone else secures it\r\n\r\nTo view and download property files: https://www.harcourtsfiles.co.nz/listings/KLIH",
